Defining two separate tasks for solving inequalities in this case does add redundancy. A single task that addresses both parts of the inequality simultaneously would be more efficient and streamlined. Here’s how such a combined task could look:

```json
{
    "owner_agent": "ProbStat",
    "tasks": {
        "SolveInequalityCombined": "Find the real values of x that satisfy -4 < x^4 + 4x^2 < 21"
    },
    "orders": [
        {
            "condition": "success",
            "from": "SolveInequalityCombined"
        }
    ],
    "refused": false,
    "answer": null
}
```

This combined task directly addresses both parts of the inequality in one step, making the TG more concise and easier to manage.
